  "question": {
    "text": "The energy of a system is given as $\\mathrm{E}(\\mathrm{t})=\\alpha^3 \\mathrm{e}^{-\\beta t}$, where t is the time and $\\beta=0.3 \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$. The errors in the measurement of $\\alpha$ and $t$ are $1.2 \\%$ and $1.6 \\%$, respectively. At $t=5 \\mathrm{~s}$, maximum percentage error in the energy is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ermh8",
      "text": "$6 \\%$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "9Nt92",
      "text": "$8.4 \\%$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "voCLO",
      "text": "$11.6 \\%$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7bhBD",
      "text": "$4 \\%$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& d E=3 \\alpha^2 d \\alpha e^{-\\beta t}+\\alpha^3 e^{-\\beta t}(-\\beta) d t \\\\\n& \\frac{d E}{E}=\\frac{3 d \\alpha}{\\alpha}+(-\\beta) d t \\\\\n& \\frac{\\Delta E}{E}=\\frac{3 \\Delta \\alpha}{\\alpha}+\\beta \\Delta t\n\\end{aligned}$\n(\\%) $\\Delta t=1.6 \\% \\times 5=8 \\%$\n$\\%\\left(\\frac{3 \\Delta \\alpha}{\\alpha}\\right)=3 \\times 1.2 \\%=3.6 \\%$\nPutting values we get\n$\\Rightarrow 3.6+8 \\times 0.3=6 \\%$",
    "image": null
  },
